INT. LAUNDROMAT - NIGHT

Humming dryers. A flickering fluorescent tube. Five people, one crowded bench.

                    ROSALIND
          That's my machine.

                    YOUNG MAN
          It was empty.

                    ROSALIND
          It was paused.

                    ABUELA TERESA
          Mija, let him have it.

                    ROSALIND
          Mama, I've been here since six.

                    TEEN GIRL
          (not looking up from phone)
          Y'all are loud.

                    YOUNG MAN
          I'm Dario, by the way.

                    ROSALIND
          I don't care, Dario.

                    ABUELA TERESA
          Dario, you want a tamale?

                    DARIO
          Yes, ma'am.

                    ROSALIND
          Mama!

                    MAN IN HOODIE
          Can someone cover me for the dryer? I need quarters.

                    TEEN GIRL
          Nobody has quarters.

                    ROSALIND
          I have quarters.

                    MAN IN HOODIE
          God bless you.

                    ROSALIND
          Take the machine, Dario.

                    DARIO
          Thank you. Really.
